From: TiogaPass BMC <bmc@tiogapass>
Date: Thu, 6 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: aspeed: silence unhandled SMBus/Gcall interrupt bits

The ASPEED I2C interrupt status register contains bits 8-12 for
SMBus-related events (General Call address match, SMBus default/device-
alt/ARP address match, and SMBus ALERT). These bits are included in
ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_RECV_MASK so the driver reads them, and the hardware
write-back at the top of the ISR clears them. However, neither the
master nor slave IRQ handler accounts for them, causing the 'irq handled
!= irq' dev_err to fire for every transaction on buses with SMBus devices.

On TiogaPass, I2C bus 5 has Infineon PXE1610 voltage regulators that
assert SMBALERT# (bit 12) after CPU power-on. This floods the kernel log
with hundreds of error messages per second, severely degrading boot
performance.

Define the missing bit constants, silently acknowledge them in the IRQ
handler, and change the remaining mismatch error to dev_err_ratelimited.

Signed-off-by: TiogaPass BMC <bmc@tiogapass>
---
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-aspeed.c	2026-03-06 20:45:04.006363955 +0000
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-aspeed.c	2026-03-06 20:48:39.206361597 +0000
@@ -70,6 +70,15 @@
 #define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_RECV_MASK			0xf000ffff
 #define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SDA_DL_TIMEOUT			BIT(14)
 #define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_BUS_RECOVER_DONE		BIT(13)
+/* Bits 8-12: SMBus/General-Call events. Included in RECV_MASK but not in
+ * INTR_ALL and not handled by master/slave IRQ handlers. Defined here so
+ * they can be silently acknowledged to prevent IRQ-mismatch log storms. */
+#define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SMBUS_ALERT			BIT(12)
+#define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SMBUS_ARP_ADDR			BIT(11)
+#define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SMBUS_DEV_ALT_ADDR		BIT(10)
+#define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SMBUS_DEF_ADDR			BIT(9)
+#define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_GCALL_ADDR			BIT(8)
+#define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SMBUS_GCALL_MASK		GENMASK(12, 8)
 #define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SLAVE_MATCH			BIT(7)
 #define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SCL_TIMEOUT			BIT(6)
 #define ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_ABNORMAL			BIT(5)
@@ -663,10 +672,15 @@
 #endif /* CONFIG_I2C_SLAVE */
 
 	irq_remaining &= ~irq_handled;
+	/* SMBus ALERT and General-Call address-match bits (8-12) are cleared
+	 * by the hardware write-back above but not handled by master/slave
+	 * handlers. Acknowledge them silently to prevent log floods from boards
+	 * where SMBus devices assert ALERT during normal operation. */
+	irq_remaining &= ~(irq_remaining & ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_SMBUS_GCALL_MASK);
 	if (irq_remaining)
-		dev_err(bus->dev,
-			"irq handled != irq. expected 0x%08x, but was 0x%08x\n",
-			irq_received, irq_handled);
+		dev_err_ratelimited(bus->dev,
+				    "irq handled != irq. expected 0x%08x, but was 0x%08x\n",
+				    irq_received, irq_handled);
 
 	/* Ack Rx done */
 	if (irq_received & ASPEED_I2CD_INTR_RX_DONE) {
